extends Node

## PART TWO: slides VII to IX of the one presentation, what the team built to work in 4D.
## Slides I to VI - how to look at it - are theatre_show_4d's and theatre_primer_4d's; the
## last of them hands the floor straight here, with no closing line and no question in
## between (Ramon, 30 Sept: "one presentation from now on"). Two slides that used to be
## here are gone - the three copies of one object, and the stop conditions - and the three
## left are the ones standing on something the team built.
##
## The audience is the October gate: Scott, Brandon, Aggelos, Nicolas, Charles - not
## designers, not 4D specialists.
##
## EVERY CLAIM CARRIES ITS TIER, because that is the rule the real deck runs on: MEASURED,
## DEMONSTRATED, OBSERVED or NOT YET MEASURED, stated rather than implied. Overclaiming has
## cost this project credibility once already and the honesty is the deck's main asset
## with this audience. Nothing here softens a gap.
##
## THE NUMBERS COME FROM THE PROGRAMME OR FROM THE EXHIBIT ITSELF, NOT FROM ME. The goat's
## and the creature's counts are read off the objects on the drum (see _fill); the walk's
## timing is the 19 Sept measurement the deck quotes. The deck is in follow_up/presentation
## temp and the rest of the record is the Notion Work Log.
##
## THE TWO EXHIBITS THAT ARE REAL WORK RATHER THAN DIAGRAM - the goat and the walking
## creature - are both ADOPTED out of the Model scene rather than invented for the
## theatre. An earlier goat WAS invented here, lofted into a wedge, and cost most of a day
## before the obvious question got asked; the rule that came out of it is that a slide
## about something the team built has to be standing on the thing the team built.

const GOAT := preload("res://ramon/chickenpen/theatre/theatre_goat_4d.gd")
const CREATURE := preload("res://ramon/chickenpen/theatre/theatre_creature_4d.gd")
const Bake := preload("res://ramon/chickenpen/theatre/theatre_bake_4d.gd")
## Part one, for the one string both parts print. A const on a script is reachable through
## the script itself, so this shares the line rather than keeping a second copy of it.
const SHOW := preload("res://ramon/chickenpen/theatre/theatre_show_4d.gd")

@export var stage_path: NodePath
@export var caption_path: NodePath
@export var show_path: NodePath
@export var presenter_path: NodePath
